A||||18||fiero56||Can't get my idle down||||8||
Z||000000||fiero56||12-17-2000||07:56 PM||||Fiero is an '86 2.8 4speed. When I start the engine cold it jumps to 2500rpm and eventually drops to 2000rpm as the engine warms, this is correct. The problem is the idle is shifted 1000rpm too high. Things I have checked or replaced. TPS, IAC, MAP, timing, EGR valve, EGR tube, cruise vac lines. Sometimes the ECM will shoot me the IAC code(45 I think), but its more of a generic code than something useful(kind of like 32).<P>Any ideas what I might be missing? I'm stumped. Makes it difficult to drive when I can spin the tires without even touching the throttle.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||terryk||12-17-2000||08:26 PM||||The code 45 is Rich Exhaust. I think you mean code 35 which is Idle Air Control. This would be right since the IAC has moved all the way in and the idle won't drop.<P>If you really checked everything for vacuum leaks, the next thing is to check the throttle physically for being held open. Disconnect the cable and verify it will close. The IAC could be bad too. When you turn off the car, do you hear it park? Zip, zip..<P>It could be the IAC is dead and isn't moving from the park position. The code would still throw.<P>Did you pinch off the brake booster hose?<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||12-17-2000||11:04 PM||||Check your what Terryk? lol....<BR>Welcome to the world of the ever present, seemingly no fix of the Fiero idle problem!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">...Possibly even more common than the squeeky alt. belt..at least close!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||12-18-2000||12:30 AM||||I haven't pinched off the brake booster, will try that tommorrow. I will also try another IAC(will pull the one off the Formula). I have triple checked for vac leakks visually, as well as with water, wd-40 and other sprayable liquids.<BR>One weird thing is the EGR valve will hold a vaccum, but if I push the diaphram up with the engine idling, there is no change in engine idling. It doesn't stumble or anything. Any ideas there?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||12-18-2000||02:28 AM||||Well, your EGR valve doesn't work... or the EGR tube could cracked wide open, which would cause a nice big vacuum leak.  Hmmm.. I just saw that you already replaced it.  I'd double check and make sure that the new one isn't already cracked.  I replaced mine almost a year ago with an OEM one and haven't had any problems with it, so I don't think it should be much of a problem.<P>Is it possible that a mechanic could have messed with the idle adjust screw sometime ago?  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||12-18-2000||11:54 AM||||I'm sure it was something cosmic! What ever you do, don't forget to check the .........<P>Sorry about that.<P>I think I meant intake and plenum gaskets. Spray some carb cleaner around there. Every high idle has been a dead IAC or a leak. Usually the EGR tube or booster hose. Sometimes a broken plastic vacuum line. I duct tape every port except the MAP port closed. If that doesn't solve it, then I spray carb cleaner. I've only seen one intake/plenum gasket failure.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||12-18-2000||06:56 PM||||I will double check the EGR tube. It is snowing and in the single digits, so I don't feel like playing in the drive tonight.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||12-22-2000||03:55 PM||||I'm feeling productive today. Finished the water pump, now on to this.<P>I double checked the EGR tube today. Removed it from the valve, it's solid and in one piece. I decided to run the engine and make sure vacuum was produced in the tube. I started the engine, it shot to 3,000rpm, I then stuck a piece of duct tape over the end of the EGR tube and idle dropped to 2,500 where it normally starts at. I lifted up on the diaphragm of the EGR valve too, it holds a vacuum and is not plugged. EGR is positively eliminated as a culprit.<P>I will try another IAC after I put everything back together, and then another TPS. The throttle is able to close fully, no obstructions, I checked the plenum gaskets, they are fine. Haven't checked the booster line yet, but my brakes do hold a vaccum even after the engine has been off for a while.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bob Englert||12-22-2000||04:24 PM||||If you lift the EGR diaphram and the engine does not stumble, then I would strongly suspect the EGR tube is plugged.  I had the same problem with one of my 87 GT's.  <P>When I removed the EGR valve I discovered the tube was broken near the EGR valve just under the insulation.  I was wondering why it was not idling high until I removed the rest of the tube.  The tube at the plenum was plugged completely with carbon and other gunk.  I think it is now time to remove the plenum and clean things out properly. I also noticed that the throttle body was very dirty.  <P>I would double check for vacuum leaks.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||12-22-2000||05:22 PM||||Fingers are thawing out again&lt;*cold!!!&gt;.<P>IAC, TPS, and brake booster can all be eliminated along with the EGR tube and valve.<P>I removed the plenum the other day, cleaned things up, looked for breaks, etc. <P>The EGR tube has plenty of vaccum and there are no breaks. Idle could be changed by plugging and unplugging the tube. The EGR valve holds a vaccume, and seems fine. I plugged the EGR tube(while disconnected from the valve), and started the engine(there was vacuum). It still started above 2,500rpm.<P>What's going on. Don't make me have to bother Ed with this one.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BOILERMAKER||12-22-2000||07:34 PM||||A high intermittent (did I spell that right, probably not) idle problem has been exhaust problems in my previous experience.  I know on one of my engines that I sold not too long ago I was suspecting an exhaust manifold and when I took it out, I found a crack in one of the manifolds right where I couldn't see it.  <P>If you have taken the EGR and EGR tube out of the lineup, you might check that next.  Worth a try I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||12-23-2000||12:41 AM||||The high idle is constant. It idles high everytime all the time. The cat on it does have a leak somewhere near it's heat shield, but a big hose clamp stopped that, and since it is downstream of the o2 sensor, I don't think it could affect idle. I don't think the car has an exhaust leak anywhere. Seems to me, it wouldn't be constant if it were an exhaust leak(expansion/contraction), could be wrong though. I'm thinking once it gets above freezing here(yeah, in like 4 months:mad <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, if I don't have any more ideas, I will just take a garden hose to it, and see if flooding all the vacuum lines changes the idle any. At least I will know a line is broken somewhere. Spray bottles and cans aren't doing it.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Uaana||12-24-2000||09:26 PM||||Excuse me but isn't a code 45 for the throttle position sensor? Seems like if that was shot or misreading you would be running rich like you describe.||||reg||1
Z||000013||fiero56||12-24-2000||09:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>The code 45 is Rich Exhaust. I think you mean code 35 which is Idle Air Control. This would be right since the IAC has moved all the way in and the idle won't drop.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||fiero56||12-24-2000||09:35 PM||||I bought another can of carb cleaner yesterday and sprayed everything on the engine that I possibly could. Idle never changed once. I'm about to rule out vaccum leak, and bas sensors. <BR>Looking at you TerryK: Is it possible for a bad ECM to cause this high idle? Possibly it isn't able to control the IAC properly? I could swap the ECM from the Formula in and try it out. The prvious owner did tell me he had ECM troubles before, and after two bad refurbs, bought a new GM unit, and had no more troubles. He didn't say what the bad ECM did, but I am running low on ideas.||||reg||1
